.\BACKEND_MODEL.md:1:# Covenant Backend Model
.\BACKEND_MODEL.md:5:This document defines the backend relational model needed to implement Covenant as a standalone backend that still fits the Automata ecosystem.
.\BACKEND_MODEL.md:20:| Spring Boot layered backend | Same layered backend | Keep `controller/service/repository/model/config` shape |
.\BACKEND_MODEL.md:35:| Workflow state | Covenant backend | `WORK_ITEMS`, `ASSIGNMENTS`, `COMMENTS`, `STATUS_HISTORY` | Covenant remains queryable without Automata joins |
.\BACKEND_MODEL.md:36:| Notification configuration and evidence | Covenant backend | `NOTIFICATION_TEMPLATES`, `NOTIFICATION_DISPATCHES`, `CONCENTRATION_NOTIFICATIONS` | Supports manual and future direct sends |
